Marilyn Barnett, played by Andrea Riseborough.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Gladys Heldman, played by Sarah Silverman.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Jack Kramer, played by Bill Pullman.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Priscilla Riggs, played by Elisabeth Shue.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Battle of the Sexes is a 2017 sports comedy-drama film directed by Valerie
Faris and Jonathan Dayton and written by Simon Beaufoy.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
The plot is loosely based on the 1973 tennis match
between Billie Jean King and Bobby Riggs.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film stars Emma Stone and Steve Carell as King and Riggs, leading an ensemble cast including Andrea Riseborough, Elisabeth
Shue, Austin Stowell, Bill Pullman, Natalie Morales, Eric Christian Olsen, and Sarah Silverman in supporting roles.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
The film marks the second collaboration between Carell and Stone after Crazy, Stupid, Love
and the second collaboration between Riseborough and Stone after Birdman.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film had its premiere at the 44th Telluride Film Festival on September 2, 2017, and was
theatrically released in the United States by Fox Searchlight Pictures on September 22, 2017.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
It received positive reviews from critics, who praised the performances of Stone and Carell
and the direction, with some calling it the best performance of Stone's career.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Despite the positive reviews, the picture performed poorly at the box
office, grossing $18.6 million against a $25 million budget.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
At the 75th Golden Globe Awards, Stone and Carell received nominations for Best Actress – Motion
Picture Musical or Comedy and Best Actor – Motion Picture Musical or Comedy respectively.

18
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
Both received Critics Choice Awards nominations in the categories
Best Actress in a Comedy and Best Actor in a Comedy.

19
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:36,000
At the 24th Screen Actors Guild Awards, Carell received a nomination for
Outstanding Performance by a Male Actor in a Supporting Role.

20
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The film explores themes of sports, tennis, 1970s, tennis player, biography.

21
01:55:30,000 --> 01:55:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
